  "details": "I know that might sound weird, but i'd actually really like an option to turn on and off the finger tracking within the settings. I have several reasons. \nOne of them, after a while of playing you just automatically let your irl-fingers idle a little, especially if you're just sitting somewhere and listen to a conversation. You don't constantly hold onto your controllers as close. This causes my fingers to either flip people off (Finger tracking creates middlefinger) or my fingers look odd in general and do weird looking poses.\nAnother reason is, it's very hard playing with avatars that have gestures connected with facial expressions on them. Yes you can turn on and off gestures with the left joystick. But if i actually do wanna use gestures, i'd always need to press down the joystick to turn them on, then several facial expressions are getting triggered from fingers being randomly recognized in certain positions etc. Just as example: I wanna do a shocked looking face, but til i am there to do that, i wasted a long time to reactivate my gestures, and then my avatar already made a silly licking face, and a angry face, til it finally makes the shocking looked facial expression.\nWith finger tracking deactivated it would only do certain expressions if you really want them, without having to toggle on gestures and having to be super careful  what your hands doing.\n\nIt's something that at least i would find very useful. I'm curious if i am the only one who thought about the same.",
